invariant: INV-41
file: rsa_mont64.c
catches: rsa_equiv_test
reason: rsa_mont64_modulus_init squares the Montgomery form of 2^(2k) four
  times where five are needed, so r2 holds the form of 2^(32k) and not of
  R, and every number it moves into the Montgomery domain is wrong by that
  factor. bin/rsa_equiv_test compares the public operation's bytes with
  the 32-bit arm's.

--- old
    for (int i = 0; i < 5; i++) {
        rsa_mont64_mont_mul(mod->r2, mod->r2, mod->r2, mod);
--- new
    for (int i = 0; i < 4; i++) {
        rsa_mont64_mont_mul(mod->r2, mod->r2, mod->r2, mod);
